From d36d951edeac59a594f95dcda89c2e93c6674343 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 05:17:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/42] RLM reachability spike: expose subagent lifecycle as a
 host tool

rlm.spawn/rlm.run (and list/collect/delete/find_models/progress_note/
create_session) were only reachable through _createKernelHostHandlers,
dispatched over the ipython kernel's comm channel -- unreachable from
a NEURA-only (baseToolsOverride) session with no kernel constructed.
The underlying methods (runRlmChild etc.) were already substrate-
neutral; only the RPC transport was kernel-bound, same shape as
agent_observe/agent_message before their Phase 1 extraction.

Adds a new "rlm" tool (tools/rlm.ts) covering the same 7 operations
the kernel bridge exposes, no new protocol invented. Wired via a new
RlmLifecycleHost interface (rlm-runtime.ts) that AgentSession already
satisfies structurally -- zero changes to _startRlmChildRun or any
other part of the deep spawn implementation. Registration in
_buildRuntime is the only agent-session.ts change: 7 net lines.

Verified two generations deep: a NEURA child can spawn its own NEURA
grandchild through the tool with no silent ipython reappearance and
no silent zero-tool child. 9 new tests; 96/96 in the edited file,
126/126 across neurabash-substrate-modes/daemon-mode/rlm-collect/
rlm-progress-notes/rlm-ledger (no regressions).

